WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.620
Some days, the hardest part is finding your
place again.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.700
Threadline keeps the context in your own
words.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:10.620
In this dementia-support scenario, an
interruption breaks a familiar routine.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.020
“What was my next planned step?”

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.100
Threadline brings back the person’s note:
“My next planned

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.300
step is to water the plant by the window.”

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:23.400
The note is a reminder, not proof that an
action happened.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.880
Now, a different moment: reflecting on the
days before a period.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.220
“What helped me feel less rushed last time?”

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:36.340
Threadline retrieves a personal observation:
leaving one evening free helped.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.400
It doesn’t decide how someone feels, or
claim that hormones caused it.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.620
They can revisit the source and add

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.120
what they want to remember next.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:47.460
These are fictional demonstrations of
today’s prototype.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.040
Live voice and wearable capture are the next
step.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.000
Threadline.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.440
A little context, kept close.
